  "question": {
    "text": "Electronic configuration of four elements $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$ and D are given below :<br />(A) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^3$<br />(B) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^4$<br />(C) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^5$<br />(D) $1 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{~s}^2 2 \\mathrm{p}^2$<br />Which of the following is the correct order of increasing electronegativity (Pauling's scale)?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WM9RD",
      "text": "A &lt; D &lt; B &lt; C",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
